WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.502
Once upon a time, there lived a married couple who desperately wanted to have a child.

2
00:00:06.503 --> 00:00:14.588
Their house overlooked a beautiful garden. Every day from her window, the wife looked down at all the flowers and herbs.

3
00:00:14.589 --> 00:00:26.698
Her favorite was the rapunzel herb. "If only I had a daughter as beautiful as that rapunzel," she wished. Finally the wife became pregnant.

4
00:00:26.699 --> 00:00:34.577
One day the wife, pointing to the rapunzel, asked her husband, "Darling, would you bring me some of those herbs?"

5
00:00:34.578 --> 00:00:40.057
"But . . . but . . . that's the witch's garden," he stammered.

6
00:00:40.058 --> 00:00:45.268
"If I don't have some rapunzel, I'll die!" she said angrily.

7
00:00:45.269 --> 00:00:48.280
Everyone was afraid of the old witch.

8
00:00:48.281 --> 00:00:52.224
She had great powers and cast spells on people.

9
00:00:52.225 --> 00:00:57.442
No one dared enter her garden, knowing they would probably not come out alive!

10
00:00:57.443 --> 00:01:01.636
The wife refused to eat anything and began to look pale.

11
00:01:01.637 --> 00:01:06.733
Worrying about her health, as well as the baby's, the husband finally gave in.

12
00:01:06.734 --> 00:01:10.422
"I'll get the herbs for you," he said.

13
00:01:10.423 --> 00:01:15.950
"Thank you, honey," she said. She blew him a kiss and clapped her hands.

14
00:01:15.951 --> 00:01:21.834
That night the husband crept into the witch's garden and stole some rapunzel.

15
00:01:21.835 --> 00:01:25.765
He brought it to his wife, who immediately ate it up.

16
00:01:25.766 --> 00:01:30.809
"Bring me fresh rapunzel every night!" she said happily.

17
00:01:30.810 --> 00:01:40.730
For a few nights after that, the husband bravely did as his wife asked until one evening, when he got caught by the witch herself.

18
00:01:40.731 --> 00:01:47.065
"So you are the thief stealing my rapunzel!" she accused angrily.

19
00:01:47.066 --> 00:01:55.393
"Please have mercy," he pleaded. "My pregnant wife said she would die if she couldn't have some."

20
00:01:55.394 --> 00:02:00.628
"Take as much as you like," the witch said, softening her voice.

21
00:02:00.629 --> 00:02:05.447
"But in return, the child born to you will be mine!"

22
00:02:05.448 --> 00:02:10.896
The husband, frightened out of his wits, had no choice but to agree.

23
00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:14.693
A few months later, a baby girl was born.

24
00:02:14.694 --> 00:02:21.803
The couple's happiness lasted only a short time because soon after, the witch appeared.

25
00:02:21.804 --> 00:02:29.958
She snatched the baby from the astonished wife and said, "I will call her Rapunzel and raise her as my own."

26
00:02:29.959 --> 00:02:34.943
Without another word, she vanished, taking Rapunzel with her.

27
00:02:34.944 --> 00:02:39.150
Rapunzel grew up to be an extremely beautiful girl.

28
00:02:39.151 --> 00:02:44.929
The witch did not want others to see her beauty, so she shut Rapunzel up in a tower.

29
00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:49.307
This tower, located in the forest, had no stairs or doors.

30
00:02:49.308 --> 00:02:52.244
There was only one way to enter it.

31
00:02:52.245 --> 00:02:59.278
"Rapunzel, Rapunzel! Let down your hair!" shouted the witch.

32
00:02:59.279 --> 00:03:02.919
From the small window dropped a thick golden rope.

33
00:03:02.920 --> 00:03:07.718
The witch climbed up the strange, shiny rope to the top of the tower.

34
00:03:07.719 --> 00:03:16.074
But in fact, it was no rope at all. Rapunzel had magnificent, long golden hair that reached past her feet.

35
00:03:16.075 --> 00:03:21.305
Whenever the witch called out, Rapunzel dropped her hair out the window.

36
00:03:21.306 --> 00:03:26.389
A few years later, the king's son happened to be riding through the forest.

37
00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:30.628
He imagined that he heard an angel singing and stopped to listen.

38
00:03:30.629 --> 00:03:35.148
"No, it's the voice of a maiden!" he realized.

39
00:03:35.149 --> 00:03:40.898
The sweet melancholy voice was coming from a tower just ahead.

40
00:03:40.899 --> 00:03:46.139
Upon seeing Rapunzel in the window, the prince fell deeply in love with her.

41
00:03:46.140 --> 00:03:49.824
He longed to go up and declare his feelings to her.

42
00:03:49.825 --> 00:03:56.083
"But how can I get inside that tower?" He was about to find out.

43
00:03:56.084 --> 00:04:05.442
He saw the witch approach the tower. "Rapunzel, Rapunzel! Let down your hair!" shouted the witch.

44
00:04:05.443 --> 00:04:10.965
The prince watched in amazement as a long golden rope descended from the window.

45
00:04:10.966 --> 00:04:19.300
The prince waited until the witch left and then called out loudly, "Rapunzel, Rapunzel! Let down your hair!"

46
00:04:19.301 --> 00:04:25.703
A few minutes later, the rope appeared, and the prince began his climb.

47
00:04:25.704 --> 00:04:31.514
Rapunzel was shocked when she saw a strange man enter through the tower window.

48
00:04:31.515 --> 00:04:35.205
"I mean no harm," the prince spoke gently.

49
00:04:35.206 --> 00:04:39.361
He confessed his feelings for her and asked if she would marry him.

50
00:04:39.362 --> 00:04:44.043
Rapunzel's heart welled with joy, and she accepted his proposal.

51
00:04:44.044 --> 00:04:47.983
Rapunzel and the prince continued to meet secretly.

52
00:04:47.984 --> 00:04:51.734
On each visit, the prince brought some silk threads.

53
00:04:51.735 --> 00:04:56.787
Rapunzel used the silk to make a rope so she could escape from the tower.

54
00:04:56.788 --> 00:05:04.433
"Rapunzel, Rapunzel! Let down your hair!" shouted the witch at her usual time.

55
00:05:04.434 --> 00:05:12.968
As she let her hair fall down, Rapunzel thought happily to herself that today would be her last day as a captive.

56
00:05:12.969 --> 00:05:17.919
In a few hours, the prince would come on his horse and . . .

57
00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:23.707
"What are you so happy about?" The witch interrupted Rapunzel's thoughts.

58
00:05:23.708 --> 00:05:28.457
"Uh . . . nothing," Rapunzel stammered.

59
00:05:28.458 --> 00:05:33.497
"What's that?" The witch pointed to something next to the bed.

60
00:05:33.498 --> 00:05:38.749
Rapunzel stared in horror as the witch held up the prince's hat.

61
00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:44.732
"Ungrateful girl! You dare deceive me?" yelled the witch.

62
00:05:44.733 --> 00:05:51.975
"I . . . I love him! We're going to get married!" Rapunzel managed to reply.

63
00:05:51.976 --> 00:05:56.686
The witch's eyes turned red as she pulled out a pair of scissors.

64
00:05:56.687 --> 00:06:03.043
Then in the blink of an eye—snip, snip!—Rapunzel's braid fell to the floor.

65
00:06:03.044 --> 00:06:07.399
The witch then banished Rapunzel to the forest.

66
00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:12.033
That evening the prince arrived, unaware of what had happened.

67
00:06:12.034 --> 00:06:17.755
"Rapunzel, Rapunzel! Let down your hair!" he called out joyfully.

68
00:06:17.756 --> 00:06:22.272
The end of the braid fell and hit his head. "Ouch!"

69
00:06:22.273 --> 00:06:28.272
The prince rubbed his head. Climbing the tower, he thought only of getting married.

70
00:06:28.273 --> 00:06:33.300
"Tonight will be the last time I . . ." Suddenly he screamed.

71
00:06:33.301 --> 00:06:39.595
Looking out the window at him was the witch. The prince was speechless.

72
00:06:39.596 --> 00:06:45.926
"So you tried to steal what's not yours!" said the witch, moving closer.

73
00:06:45.927 --> 00:06:51.384
Before she could cast a spell on him, the prince let go of Rapunzel's hair.

74
00:06:51.385 --> 00:06:55.256
He fell into a thorny bush that pierced his eyes.

75
00:06:55.257 --> 00:06:59.728
Blinded, the prince got on his horse and took off for the forest.

76
00:06:59.729 --> 00:07:03.633
Days turned to weeks, and weeks turned to months.

77
00:07:03.634 --> 00:07:07.485
The blind prince searched and searched for his beloved.

78
00:07:07.486 --> 00:07:10.496
He could find no trace of Rapunzel.

79
00:07:10.497 --> 00:07:18.573
After several years the prince was about to give up and return to his palace when he heard a familiar sound.

80
00:07:18.574 --> 00:07:24.758
"Rapunzel? Is that you?" he called out toward the sweet singing voice.

81
00:07:24.759 --> 00:07:30.130
The singing stopped abruptly, and the woman turned around.

82
00:07:30.131 --> 00:07:34.268
"My prince, you found me!" she cried.

83
00:07:34.269 --> 00:07:39.683
As tears of joy ran down his face, the prince saw a bright light.

84
00:07:39.684 --> 00:07:46.336
True love reopened his eyes. Not even the witch's hate could separate them forever.

85
00:07:46.337 --> 00:07:56.639
The prince took Rapunzel back to his palace, and they lived happily ever after.

